# How to Deploy Your AI Model to IntelliWare

## PART 1 — Export from Google Teachable Machine

### Step 1: Open your Teachable Machine project
Go to [teachablemachine.withgoogle.com](https://teachablemachine.withgoogle.com) and open the project you already trained.

### Step 2: Click "Export Model"
At the top-right of the page, click the **Export Model** button.

### Step 3: Choose TensorFlow.js format
In the popup:
1. Click the **TensorFlow.js** tab at the top.
2. Make sure **"Quantized"** conversion type is selected (it's the default).
3. Click the **"Download my model"** button (NOT "Upload").

> [!IMPORTANT]
> You must click **Download** — not Upload. Uploading gives you a hosted URL which will NOT work offline or on your local XAMPP server.

### Step 4: Extract the downloaded ZIP
A file called something like `converted_keras.zip` or `my_model.zip` will download to your `C:\Users\YourName\Downloads` folder.

Right-click the ZIP file → **Extract All** → Click **Extract**.

After extraction, open the folder. You should see exactly **3 files** inside:
```
model.json
metadata.json
weights.bin
```

> [!WARNING]
> If you see a `.h5` file or a `saved_model` folder instead, you chose the **wrong format** (Keras or TensorFlow — not TensorFlow.js). Go back to Step 3 and pick the **TensorFlow.js** tab.

---

## PART 2 — Copy the files into IntelliWare

### Step 5: Open the destination folder
Open **File Explorer** (Windows key + E).

In the address bar at the top, click it and paste this path exactly:
```
C:\xampp\htdocs\IntelliWare\uploads\tm_models\global
```
Press **Enter**.

The `global` folder should open and it should be **empty** (I already created it for you).

> [!NOTE]
> If you get "Folder not found", open `C:\xampp\htdocs\IntelliWare\uploads\tm_models\` and manually create a new folder called `global` inside it.

### Step 6: Copy your 3 model files
Go back to the folder where you extracted the ZIP in Step 4.

Select all 3 files:
- `model.json`
- `metadata.json`
- `weights.bin`

**Copy them** (Ctrl + C), then go back to the `global` folder and **Paste** (Ctrl + V).

Your folder should now look like this:
```
C:\xampp\htdocs\IntelliWare\uploads\tm_models\global\
    ├── model.json       ✅
    ├── metadata.json    ✅
    └── weights.bin      ✅
```

---

## PART 3 — Test in IntelliWare

### Step 7: Refresh the page
Go back to your browser and press **F5** (or Ctrl + R) to refresh the Receive Inventory page.

### Step 8: Click "Start AI Scanner"
Click the green **Start AI Scanner** button.

- The browser will ask for **camera permission** — click **Allow**.
- The camera will open and start scanning immediately.
- The moment it sees a product, it will **instantly** identify it and add it to the transaction.

> [!TIP]
> If you still see "Model error: 404" after refreshing, double-check that the files are in the **exact** path: `global\model.json` — not inside a sub-folder like `global\my_model\model.json`.
